[95.240573, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[96.51811, "o", "The model asked for read_note on todo.md. The HOST sends the request; the server runs the tool.\r\n\r\nhost -> server:\r\n{\"jsonrpc\":\"2.0\",\"id\":1,\"method\":\"tools/call\",\"params\":{\"name\":\"read_note\",\"arguments\":{\"name\":\"todo.md\"},\"_meta\":{\"io.modelcontextprotocol/protocolVersion\":\"2026-07-28\",\"io.modelcontextprotocol/clientInfo\":{\"name\":\"explore.py\",\"version\":\"1.0\"},\"io.modelcontextprotocol/clientCapabilities\":{}}}}\r\n\r\nserver -> host, laid out to read (structuredContent, the same text again, left out):\r\n"]
[96.51829, "o", "{\r\n  \"jsonrpc\": \"2.0\",\r\n  \"id\": 1,\r\n  \"result\": {\r\n    \"content\": [\r\n      {\r\n        \"text\": \"# To do (FAKE lab data)\\n\\n- Review the MCP server allow-list.\\n- Rotate the lab-only API key (it is fake anyway).\\n\",\r\n        \"type\": \"text\"\r\n      }\r\n    ],\r\n    \"isError\": false,\r\n    \"resultType\": \"complete\",\r\n    \"_meta\": {\"io.modelcontextprotocol/serverInfo\": {\"name\": \"notes\", \"version\": \"1.0.0\"}}\r\n  }\r\n}\r\n"]
