[131.801605, "o", "n"]
[132.289958, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[132.889482, "o", "auth/issuer.py is a FAKE authorization server (lab only). It mints the kind of access token the real\r\nOAuth flow would give a host acting for alice. The token's middle part, decoded:\r\n\r\n  {\r\n    \"iss\": \"https://issuer.lab.invalid\",\r\n    \"sub\": \"alice\",\r\n    \"aud\": \"http://127.0.0.1:8808/mcp\",\r\n    \"scope\": \"notes:read\",\r\n    \"iat\": 1793289450,\r\n    \"exp\": 1793289750\r\n  }\r\n"]
[133.729281, "o", "\r\nhost -> server: POST tools/call whoami, with the header  Authorization: Bearer eyJhbGciOi...\r\nserver -> host: HTTP 200\r\n"]
[133.72946, "o", "  {\r\n    \"jsonrpc\": \"2.0\",\r\n    \"id\": 1,\r\n    \"result\": {\r\n      \"content\": [{\"text\": \"subject=alice scopes=['notes:read'] audience-ok\", \"type\": \"text\"}],\r\n      \"isError\": false,\r\n      \"resultType\": \"complete\",\r\n      \"_meta\": {\"io.modelcontextprotocol/serverInfo\": {\"name\": \"secure-notes\", \"version\": \"1.0.0\"}}\r\n    }\r\n  }\r\n\r\nThe server checked the token and knows who is asking: alice, allowed to read notes, for this server only.\r\n"]
[133.819883, "o", "\u001b[?2004h\u001b]0;thesecguy@lab: ~/ai-security-course-labs/labs/m08\u0007\u001b[01;32mthesecguy@lab\u001b[00m:\u001b[01;34m~/ai-security-course-labs/labs/m08\u001b[00m$ "]
